    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on upgrading the security protocols for a mid-sized law firm. We're moving away from SMS-based MFA because of the interception risks and want to implement hardware security keys (like YubiKeys) instead. Can you give me a step-by-step guide on how to handle the deployment and the user onboarding process? We need it to be as seamless as possible so the partners don't complain.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To deploy hardware security keys, start by assessing your current MFA setup and identifying potential pain points. Begin the deployment process by replacing SMS-based MFA with hardware keys for all employees who will use them. This typically involves purchasing the keys, configuring them with your organization's settings, and providing employee support for setup and troubleshooting. You can also take this opportunity to update your company's MFA policies and procedures. A phased rollout may be necessary to minimize disruption.",
